                        "sense_id": "94879659-3fd3-38f2-8b3a-92621bac1ff6",
                        "entry_id": "3525c2c0-257b-31e1-89c7-8856660c7743",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Advocating or working towards a solution to some problem (often used to imply that no simple solution exists)."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "derogatory",
                            "often"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "dd22d2b1-320c-49d9-ae88-71728378aff3",
                                "sense_id": "94879659-3fd3-38f2-8b3a-92621bac1ff6",
                                "text": "The ideology of solutionism is thus essential to helping Silicon Valley maintain its image. The technology press — along with the meme-hustlers at the TED conference — are only happy to play up any solutionist undertakings."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "48517613-c40f-4905-94cf-a49cdab2a068",
                                "sense_id": "94879659-3fd3-38f2-8b3a-92621bac1ff6",
                                "text": "Some promote MOOCS as the future of lower-cost higher eduction, while others lament them a solutionist privatization of educational practice."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "2642a934-0c50-437a-9ec7-3d704b6bb7ad",
                                "sense_id": "94879659-3fd3-38f2-8b3a-92621bac1ff6",
                                "text": "Silicon Valley prides itself on a solutionist worldview. Founders are told to think of a problem and then build a company that solves it. They invent problems no one has just to say it's been fixed."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
